/// Data for a database, declared in the project: seeds/*.yaml, applied by
/// <app> seed through the model's use cases (its validations, its
/// defaults). Records written out (categories, settings), each with an
/// alias ($id) others point at, and records generated by the hundred for
/// demos (generate: 500, with rules per field: dates in the past, amounts
/// in a range, values by weight), the same every time. Applying again
/// keeps what is there; --fresh starts over; production is refused.
blueprint seed {
  version "0.1.0"
  requires app, env, domain, postgres, migrations, store
  optional rest
  go_require "go.yaml.in/yaml/v3" "v3.0.6"
}
